# ---------- Go ----------
bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
*.prof
# Per-machine workspace files.
go.work
go.work.sum

# ---------- Frontend (Vite / React / TS) ----------
node_modules
ui/dist/
ui/.vite/
# tsc -b build-mode stamp file, written by the UI typecheck.
ui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# The SPA is built into the Go binary's embed dir. The placeholder lives at
# backend/web/placeholder.html instead, so `vite build`'s emptyOutDir never
# clobbers a tracked file. Only .gitkeep belongs in git here — it keeps the
# directory embeddable via //go:embed before the first build ever runs.
backend/web/dist/*
!backend/web/dist/.gitkeep

# ---------- SQLite ----------
# The WAL sidecars are as untrackable as the database itself, and a bare
# *.db rule leaves them staged by an unlucky `git add -A`.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---------- Runtime data ----------
# The database, and the repositories rongo clones in order to index them.
# Those clones are other people's source code — never this repo's content.
/data/
/repos/

# ---------- Secrets ----------
.env
# Any .env variant — backups, per-host copies, editor swap files. A bare `.env`
# rule leaves `.env.bak`/`.env.local` untracked-but-committable, which is how
# real API keys and repository PATs get staged. `.env.example` carries no
# secrets and is re-included.
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------- Test & coverage output ----------
coverage/
coverage.out
coverage.xml
*.cobertura.xml
# Playwright run output.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# ---------- Agent & editor tooling ----------
# Local Claude Code settings, and the worktrees that live under .claude/.
.claude/
.superpowers/
# Playwright MCP scratch output, written to the repo root during browser-driven
# UI verification.
.playwright-mcp/

# ---------- Deliverables written for reading, not for the repo ----------
# A few design documents under docs/plans/ are deliberately force-added
# (`git add -f`) and tracked despite this rule — keep the rule; a new document
# meant to be kept needs the same `git add -f`.
docs/plans/

# ---------- Stray images at the repo root ----------
# Verification screenshots land here during UI work. They are throwaway
# evidence and may show a logged-in session or proprietary source code on
# screen — an unlucky `git add -A` must not commit one. The wordmark is the
# one image that genuinely belongs at the root.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
!/rongo-wide.png

# ---------- OS & editors ----------
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# The live repository list. repos.example.yaml is the tracked template; this is
# the operator's own copy and carries real clone URLs and token_env names for
# internal forges. Same leak class the .env rules above guard against.
repos.yaml
